{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Avenge the vengeance of the children of Israel from the Midianites; afterward you shall be gathered to your people.</b> For I do not regret my oath that I swore (ibid.) — therefore you shall not bring me in (to the land). Therefore this was juxtaposed to the section concerning the vows of an ordinary person, who may come to regret." "<b>Afterward you shall be gathered.</b> Some say: you shall see and rejoice in the vengeance of your enemies. And they said in the Midrash: the Holy One, blessed be He, said <b>the vengeance of the children of Israel</b>, and Moses said <b>the vengeance of HaShem</b>. Moses said to the Holy One, blessed be He: Master of the Universe, if we had been uncircumcised or idolaters, they would not hate us; and on what account do they hate us? On account of the Torah and the commandments that You gave us — the vengeance is Yours. Therefore it says ״לתת נקמת ה׳ במדין״ — to give the vengeance of HaShem in Midian; for whoever stands against Israel is as though he stands against the Holy One, blessed be He." "<b>From the Midianites.</b> But were not the Moabites first in the matter, as it says (Numbers 22:7) ״וילכו זקני מואב וזקני מדין״? Rather, the Moabites entered into the matter only out of fear, as it says (ibid.) ״ויגר מואב מפני העם״ — that they (the Israelites) would not plunder them, for it was said only (Deuteronomy 2:9) ״ואל תתגר בם מלחמה״ — do not provoke war with them. But the Midianites took offense over a quarrel that was not theirs; and furthermore, David was destined to come forth from Ruth the Moabitess."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:37:12.789205902Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}